 "notes_ja": "キーはD（イントロとAはCナチュラルのDミクソリディアン、BはF#が出るDメジャー）。イントロ（1〜11小節）はD5のドローンだけで、7小節目からバイオリンのメロディ、11小節目後半にドラムのフィル。A（12〜21）は「D5｜D5 Csus2」の2小節パターンを3回→Am7（2小節）→D→G。B（22〜34）はD｜G｜Bm Asus4｜G｜D｜Asus4 Esus4のあと、3小節のリフレイン「Bm｜G｜D Asus4」を2回くり返し、34小節目のDの途中で動画が終わります。伴奏はDとAの開放弦のようなドローンが鳴り続けて3度がほとんど聞こえないため、5・sus表記にしています（普通のD・C・A・Eで弾いても大きくは外れません）。",
 "method": "Root: per dotted-quarter beat, harmonic-summed salience (f0+0.5*oct+0.3*12th) of a 36-bin/oct CQT of bass.wav (E1-B4), aggregated per half bar (first beat weighted 1.5); intro bars 1-11 have no bass, root taken from the sustained D3 drone in other.wav. Quality: violin removed from other.wav by tracking its f0 with the basic-pitch contour (argmax >= F#4) and notching harmonics k*f0 (+-0.6 st) in the STFT; per-half-bar pitch-class energy of the residual in E2-B4 (accompaniment) and E2-C6, plus whole-mix chroma (E2-C7) as cross-check; cosine template matching with root fixed to the bass root over 5/maj/min/sus2/sus4/7/m7/7sus4, then a musical check (D mixolydian / D major). Tuning measured ~+5..+10 cents (concert pitch). Findings: backing voicings are open (D-A drones everywhere): D chords = D5 (no F#) in intro and A; F# only appears from bar 20 and in B (mostly melody/upper part), so B D chords written 'D'. G chords = G5/Gadd9 backing + B in melody -> 'G'. Bm clearly minor (D natural + F#). A chords in B: no C# anywhere, D present -> 'Asus4'. 27b E: A on top, neither G nor G# -> 'Esus4' (low confidence). 18-19: A bass + G3 (+C4, no E), melody C5/B4/D5 -> 'Am7' (G/A or A7sus4 equally plausible in the low register; low confidence). 21b: bass slides G->E->D under a held G5 voicing -> 'Em7' (= G6; could be written G). Bass passing tones (not chord changes): 25 beat4 D, 28 beat4 A, 29 beat4 F#, 31 beat4 A, 32 beat4 D/E. Check: synthesized chord pads (root + chord tones) vs chroma of (violin-masked other + bass) per half bar, mean cosine: intro 0.882, A 0.906, B 0.896 (plain triads 0.867/0.877/0.892; all-D5 0.882/0.708/0.535); no half bar below 0.6. Chord-tone overlays inspected over the CQT for bars 11-34. Uncertain: qualities of 18-19 (Am7 vs G/A), 21b (Em7 vs G), 27b (Esus4), and whether B-section D/G chords voice the 3rd in the backing.",
 "reconciled": "Reconciled with bass/pad/guitar/drums/harmony: one chord list and one sections list for all parts (see chords.json). Chord decisions checked on the violin-notched accompaniment (guitar/accomp.wav), the other-stem side channel and the bass stem: 13b/15b/17b = Csus2 (C4+G4 loudest, the D3 pedal keeps sounding ~17 dB below); bars 18-19 = one Am7 (bass A1 tied, pad D3-G3 tied over the barline, C4 tail still ~8 dB above the floor in 19a, so no chord change at bar 19); bar 21 = G for the whole bar (backing G3-D4-G4, no E or B; bass E2 is a one-quarter passing note at pos 8); 27b Esus4 kept (A2/A3/E on top of bass E2, no G/G#, no B). Grid-shift test of every part against its stem: best at 0 (no part offset by a grid step). harmony.json was edited after harmony/write.py ran; rerunning write.py would undo these edits."
